# DTF tier manifest: db-keepalive-startup-retry  (artifact-keeper#4549, fixed by
# #4695, 1.11.2)
# Profile-set: filesystem + db.keepalive-off-peer (a second backend on the same
# Postgres with DATABASE_TCP_KEEPALIVES=false, on its own address).
#
# THE BUG (#4549)
# A force-killed backend pod left its Postgres sessions open for the OS's ~2 h
# TCP keepalive default; across replicas the ghosts filled max_connections and
# the replacement pod died on its first `Sqlx(PoolTimedOut)` at boot and
# crash-looped for hours. The fix arms tcp_keepalives_idle=15 / interval=5 /
# count=3 with a query right after connect on every pooled session (opt out:
# DATABASE_TCP_KEEPALIVES=false), retries the initial pool connect up to five
# times with a jittered 1-8 s backoff (about 40 s with the defaults) instead of
# exiting, and counts failures in ak_db_pool_connection_failures_total{stage}.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   * Keepalives are a per-session SERVER setting, so `SHOW` on another
#     session cannot see them; the kernel can. `ss -to` in a throwaway
#     netshoot container in the Postgres netns prints each 5432 socket's
#     keepalive timer: <= 15 s on an armed session, ~119 min (the 7200 s
#     kernel default) otherwise. Sessions are attributed to a backend by peer
#     IP, which is why backend-nokeep has its own address.
#   * The boot outage: `docker stop` the backend, `docker pause` this slot's
#     own Postgres (the kernel still accepts the TCP connect, the server never
#     answers, so each attempt ends in the 5 s acquire timeout: PoolTimedOut),
#     `docker start` the backend, `docker unpause` 12 s later. An EXIT trap
#     unpauses Postgres if the oracle dies mid-outage.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (CONTROL) both images: both backends hold established sessions that carry
#             a keepalive timer; the DATABASE_TCP_KEEPALIVES=false peer's timers
#             are all >= 60 min, before and after the outage, and it still
#             serves; the docker pause took; with Postgres up a restarted
#             backend comes up and serves an authenticated request.
#   (FIX)     every session of the default backend has a timer <= 15 s; the
#             backend booted during the 12 s freeze comes up by itself; its
#             log has "database pool: initial connect attempt 1/5 failed ...
#             retrying". RED on 1.11.1: timers ~119 min, the container exits
#             on the first PoolTimedOut, no retry line.
#   (FIX #4828, a KNOWN-RED pin until #4888) ak_db_pool_connection_failures_total
#             {stage="startup"} is >= 1 after the failed boot attempts. RED on
#             1.11.4: never exported, the retry counted before main.rs
#             installed the Prometheus recorder.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle logs in again after every restart.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem db.keepalive-off-peer"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
